      "name": null,
      "problem": "${\\text{i}}^{24}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the value of $\\text{i}$ raised to some positive integer power $n$, we divide $n$ by $4,$ and raise $\\text{i}$ to the remainder.\n\nIn our case, we have $n=24.$ Dividing the power by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n24÷4=6\\,\\text{R}0.\n$$\n\nSo the remainder is $0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{24}={\\text{i}}^{0}=1.\n$$",
