      "problem": "Simplify ${\\text{i}}^{50}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the value of $\\text{i}$ raised to some positive integer power $n$, we divide $n$ by $4,$ and raise $\\text{i}$ to the remainder.\n\nIn our case, we have $n=50.$ Dividing the power by $4,$ we get:\n\n$$\n50÷4=12\\,\\text{R}2\n$$\n\nSo the remainder is $2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{50}={\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.\n$$",
