      "name": null,
      "problem": "${\\text{i}}^{-1}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, using the laws of exponents, we can write\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{\\text{i}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the numerator and denominator by $\\text{i},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\text{i}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{i}}{\\text{i}}=\\frac{\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now recall that ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}=\\frac{\\text{i}}{(-1)}=-\\text{i}.\n$$",
